class.description:
The server passes this request to the handler declared with [method Netw.configure_admission], after every [NetwAccountProvider] has verified. The joining client is not connected until the handler calls [method admit], and [method NetwRequest.deny] tells it why it was refused. The player reads the code and the reason in [signal NetwSession.join_failed] and [signal NetwConnection.failed]. The reason is cut to 255 UTF-8 bytes, and an empty one sends a default sentence that names the code. A handler that finishes without calling either refuses the join with [constant @GlobalScope.ERR_UNAUTHORIZED] and reports an error. The handler may [code]await[/code], and what it returns is ignored. A requested [member username] does not verify an account.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
func admit(request: NetwJoinRequest) -> void:
    if request.account:
        request.admit()
    else:
        request.deny()
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
void Admit(NetwJoinRequest request)
{
    if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(request.Account))
        request.Deny();
    else
        request.Admit();
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
